+## Machine-readable runbook of this flow
+
+The layers below are also available as a generated, machine-readable runbook,
+`runbooks/push-path.v1.json` in the plugin (next to the runbooks of the start,
+plan, implement and close paths and their `index.v1.json`). It is generated by
+`scripts/generate-runbook.mjs` from the command tables, never written by hand,
+and a Verify suite fails when a command, flag or step changes without the
+runbook being regenerated. The first call of a standard command (the start
+preflight, `pipeline-state.mjs inspect` and `submit-plan`, the close
+coordinator's `drive`, `push-prepare.mjs` and `push-init.mjs`) returns a typed
+`runbook` field `{ path, digest, step }` that names the runbook of its path and
+the step the command is; it appears once per session and path, and always on a
+refusal. The field is additive: every other result field is unchanged.
+
